<programme start="20261014013300 +0000" stop="20261014021600 +0000" channel="AMC+ 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Eli Roth&apos;s History of Horror</title><sub-title lang="en">Zombies</sub-title><desc lang="en">Zombies are the monsters of the 21st century, and America&apos;s major contribution to horror; a look at what set off zombie fever leads to George Romero, who made zombies a metaphor for social ills.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-MA</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15814493_b_v12_ag.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261014021600 +0000" stop="20261014030000 +0000" channel="AMC+ 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Eli Roth&apos;s History of Horror</title><sub-title lang="en">Slashers, Part 1</sub-title><desc lang="en">Slasher films make a killing in the &apos;80s, but their violence, perceived misogyny and endless sequels almost end the genre; supernatural killers Chucky and Freddy save them from extinction.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-MA</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15814493_b_v12_ag.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261014030000 +0000" stop="20261014034300 +0000" channel="AMC+ 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Eli Roth&apos;s History of Horror</title><sub-title lang="en">Slashers, Part 2</sub-title><desc lang="en">The evolution of slashers, from Freddy Krueger to Candyman to the terrifying Hannibal Lecter in the &apos;90s, to torture porn in the 2000s as a response to post-9/11 panic.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-MA</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15814493_b_v12_ag.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261014034300 +0000" stop="20261014042600 +0000" channel="AMC+ 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Eli Roth&apos;s History of Horror</title><sub-title lang="en">The Demons Inside</sub-title><desc lang="en">The fear that demons will enter one&apos;s body and make one do terrible things inspires some of the most frightening films ever made, including the masterpieces</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-14</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15814493_b_v12_ag.jpg"/></programme>
<programme start="20261014042600 +0000" stop="20261014050900 +0000" channel="AMC+ 🇺🇸"><title lang="en">Eli Roth&apos;s History of Horror</title><sub-title lang="en">Killer Creatures</sub-title><desc lang="en">Monsters hold a special place in the history of horror as the killer predators in nature; the nightmare creatures of the fantastic are waiting to escape.</desc><category lang="en">Documentary</category><rating system="MPA"><value>TV-14</value></rating><icon src="https://cdn.tvpassport.com/image/show/960x540/v2/p15814493_b_v12_ag.jpg"/></programme>
